        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Safari 26.2 partially supports scrollend event]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28664</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28664"/>
        <updated>2025-12-14T21:00:36.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>

<p dir="auto">Safari 26.2 partially supports <code class="notranslate">scrollend</code> event but still marked as Tech Preview only</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>

<p dir="auto">Test here:<br>
<a href="https://codepen.io/web-dot-dev/pen/OJdxKqJ" rel="nofollow">https://codepen.io/web-dot-dev/pen/OJdxKqJ</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Or run these:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">'onscrollend' in HTMLElement.prototype<br>
&lt; true<br>
'onscrollend' in Document.prototype<br>
&lt; true<br>
'onscrollend' in VisualViewport.prototype<br>
&lt; false</p>
</blockquote>
<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526265277-3e056cb5-d06d-44e1-aca5-b3368fcb2da2.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..tryhXKiusfIcC4948rWchRb66zAYhpkDWInJ8pxZi4I"><img width="528" height="215" alt="image" src="https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526265277-3e056cb5-d06d-44e1-aca5-b3368fcb2da2.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..tryhXKiusfIcC4948rWchRb66zAYhpkDWInJ8pxZi4I" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 215px;"></a>

<p dir="auto">Also noted here: <a href="https://webkit.org/blog/17640/webkit-features-for-safari-26-2/#:~:text=Safari%2026.2%20adds%20support%20for%20the%20scrollend%20event" rel="nofollow">https://webkit.org/blog/17640/webkit-features-for-safari-26-2/#:~:text=Safari%2026.2%20adds%20support%20for%20the%20scrollend%20event</a></p>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>

]]></content>
